{"k":"gap","w":1368},
{"k":"p","w":1368,"r":[{"t":"That means all of this processing must happen in:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1377},
{"k":"p","w":1377,"r":[{"t":"0.2 seconds"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1379},
{"k":"p","w":1379,"r":[{"t":"So we divide."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1382},
{"k":"p","w":1382,"r":[{"t":"Pixel operations in 0.2s: 2.34 billion ÷ 5 around and equal to 468 million operations in 200 ms","b":1}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1400},
{"k":"p","w":1400,"r":[{"t":"That is:"}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1402},
{"k":"p","w":1402,"r":[{"t":"~2.34 billion ops per second sustained ~468 million ops per reaction window"}]},
{"k":"p","w":1414,"r":[{"t":"And this is low balling everything."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1420},
{"k":"p","w":1420,"r":[{"t":"At age fourteen, this observation feat becomes fundamentally different from the same task at age five, not because the environment changes, but because the way his brain handles information has been radically compressed through nine uninterrupted years of White Room conditioning. The key shift is that he no longer perceives the scene as a collection of separate details. Instead, he recognizes structured patterns instantly. Human movement, spacing, posture, timing, and environmental consistency are no longer processed one by one. They are processed as unified packets. This drastically reduces cognitive overhead while increasing accuracy. On top of that, his attention is no longer evenly distributed. He anticipates where irregularities are statistically most likely to appear, meaning most of his processing power is focused on high value zones rather than wasted on neutral background information."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1553},
{"k":"p","w":1553,"r":[{"t":"By fourteen, his reaction window also tightens. The fear conditioning, punishment based correction, and repetition push perceptual decision making well below average adult reaction times. He is not reacting after the fact. He is recognizing and validating anomalies almost as soon as the visual input stabilizes. This allows him to scan dense urban scenes in fractions of a second without panic, hesitation, or loss of detail. The result is not superhuman vision, but superhuman interpretation speed. His eyes remain human. His brain is simply no longer bottlenecked by hesitation, indecision, or sequential processing."}]},
{"k":"gap","w":1646},
{"k":"p","w":1646,"r":[{"t":"What makes this feat extreme is that it is sustainable. This is not a burst of focus or a lucky moment. It is a trained baseline state. He can repeat this level of observation continuously under stress, motion sickness, and threat of punishment. That consistency is what elevates the feat from impressive perception to elite level cognitive processing. By fourteen, the same task that once required conscious effort has become automatic, faster, and far denser in informational output."}]},
